senses.gloss:
--a sacred place in कालसर्पी;
1: Br. III. १३. ९९.
on the slopes of the मुण्डपृष्ठ;
2: वा. २३. १९५; १०८. ६६.
a तीर्थम् sacred to पुष्टि.
3: M. १३. ४७.

--as opposed to पितृयान; the north road of the sun, situated to the north of नागवीथि and south of the सप्तऋषिश्; here live Siddhas and they have no rebirths;
1: वा. ५०. २१६; Vi. II. 8. ९०-7.
reached through the पिन्गल passage (on the right side of the body);
2: भा. II. 2. २४ [2]; Br. II. २१. १६९.
four roads to and the door of the sun leading to them;
3: Br. I. 7. १८३.
शिबि's lavish gifts to attain देवयान.
4: M. ४२. १९-20.

(I)--a Siddha, and a son of धिषणा and कृशाश्व, and identified with Hari;
1: भा. VI. 6. २०; १५. १२; XI. १६. २८.
came to see परिक्षित् practising प्रायोपवेश;
2: Ib. I. १९. १०.
knew the yoga power of विष्णु;
3: Ib. II. 7. ४५.
told शुक्र the story of Citraketu;
4: Ib. VI. १४. 9.
cursed हूहू to be born a crocodile;
5: Ib. VIII. 4. 3.
did not comprehend Hari's माय,
6: Ib. IX. 4. ५७.
came to see कृष्ण at स्यमन्तपञ्चक;
7: Ib. X. ८४. 3.
a ब्रह्मवादिन्;
8: M. १४५. १०७.
exclusion of marriage alliances with कश्यपस् and Asitas.
9: Ib. १९९. १९.

--is Skanda;
1: Br. III. १०. ५०; ७३. ११०.
anointed by all the Devas and their गणस्;
2: वा. ३९. ३३; ७२. ४९.
as विष्णु.
3: Vi. I. 8. २८.

--the homes of the nine planets;
1: Br. II. २३. ९५; वा. ५२. ८५.
temples visited by परशुराम;
2: Br. III. २४. ४१; २७. ११; IV. ३८. ५७; M. ९६. २५; २५७. 6.
see also देवगृहस्.
